      "dom_id": "question-67655",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to 3}{log}_{3}⁡(x-3).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{3}⁡(x-3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273970/assets/91e0a0ebd65df128534d58d181e62be18aa1c398cf526da7838d1a56e62f7d08.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>3.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are not equal, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
